These are the names of the ancestors of Jesus Christ, son of David, son of Abraham:
Ibrahim, son of Isaac, and Isaac, son of Jacob, and Jacob, son of Judah and his brothers.
And Judah fathered Perez and Zerah by Tamar, and Perez fathered Hezron, and Hezron fathered Aram.
And Aram was the father of Aminadab, and Aminadab was the father of Nahshon, and Nahshon was the father of Salmon,
and Salmon fathered Boaz by Rahab, and Boaz fathered Obed by Ruth, and Obed fathered Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. And David was the son of Solomon from the woman he was married to, Uriah.
And Solomon was the father of Rehoboam, and Rehoboam was the father of Abijah, and Abijah was the father of Asa.
And Asa begot Jehoshaphat, and Jehoshaphat begot Jehoram, and Jehoram begot Uzziah,
And Uzziah begot Jotham, and Jotham begot Ahaz, and Ahaz begot Hezekiah,
And Hezekiah begot Manasseh, and Manasseh begot Amon, and Amon begot Josiah,
And Josiah was the son of Jehoiakim, and his brothers, at the time when the Jews were exiled to the land of Babylon.
And after they returned to the Jews from Babylon, Kenaniah begat Shealtiel, and Shealtiel begat Zerubbabel.
And Zerubbabel begat Abiud, and Abiud begat Eliakim, and Eliakim begat Azor,
And Azor was the father of Sadok, and Sadok was the father of Akhim, and Akhim was the father of Eliud.
And Eliud begot Eleazar, and Eleazar begot Matthan, and Matthan begot Jacob,
And Jacob was the father of Joseph, the husband of Mary, who gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
All the generations from Abraham to David were fourteen generations, and from David to the time of the exile of the Jews to Babylon were fourteen generations, and from the time they were exiled to Babylon until the birth of Christ were fourteen generations. The birth of Jesus Christ.
And this was the birth of Jesus Christ: When Mary was betrothed to Joseph, before they came together, she was found to be with child by the Holy Spirit. Luke
And Joseph, her fiancé, was a righteous man and did not want to expose her, and decided to divorce her quietly.
And while he was thinking about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream and said: “Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary as your wife, because what she carries within her is from the Holy Spirit.
And she will give birth to a son, and you shall name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.” Luke
And all of this happened so that the word of God would be fulfilled through the tongue of the prophet who said:
“Behold, the young woman shall conceive and bear a son, and they shall name him Emmanuel,” which means: God is with us.
